@startuml
' Figure 7.6  Rebooking saga with compensations
' Reading order: top to bottom. Each step is its own keyed effect. A
' failure before the pivot runs the compensations in reverse; after
' the pivot nothing is undone, so the pivot comes last but one.
!include plantuml-theme.puml
start
:Hold new seat;
note right: undo: release hold
:Charge fare difference;
note right: undo: refund
:Issue new ticket;
note right: undo: void same day
if (all three committed?) then (yes)
  :Cancel old segment (pivot);
  :Notify traveler;
  stop
else (no)
  :Run undo steps in reverse;
  :Traveler keeps old seat;
  stop
endif
@enduml
